# Cloudflare Workers static-assets header rules.
#
# Copied verbatim into dist/ by Astro at build time (public/ passthrough) and
# parsed by Workers — it is not served as an asset itself. Rules here OVERRIDE
# the Content-Type Cloudflare would otherwise infer.
#
# Why this file exists: agent-facing text files (llms.txt and the per-page .md
# mirrors) were served without a charset, so clients fell back to Latin-1 and
# UTF-8 CJK bytes rendered as mojibake (部署 -> éƒ¨ç½²). Declaring charset=utf-8
# on every text-ish response fixes that at the wire level. HTML pages already
# carry <meta charset>, so their entry is belt-and-braces only.
#
# Match by URL path (not MIME type): the more specific /llms.txt rule precedes
# the /*.txt glob so it wins unambiguously.

/llms.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

/*.md
  Content-Type: text/markdown; charset=utf-8

/*.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

/*.xml
  Content-Type: application/xml; charset=utf-8

/*.html
  Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8
